          "en": "7. Estimated harvesting period: from ....... month ....... year ...... to ..... month ..... year .....\n.........., day .... month ...... year .....\nFOREST OWNER\n(Sign, state full name)\nNote:\n(*) This form shall be used by forest owners or owners of forest products that\nare individuals, family households or residential communities (abbreviated as the\nforest owner) when formulating the plan for harvesting timber and non-timber forest\nplants of ordinary species/collection of specimens of ordinary forest plant species.\nI. INFORMATION ON THE FOREST OWNER\n(1) Record the specific harvesting case in accordance with the\nprovisions of clause 2 or clause 7 of Article 6 of this Circular.\n(2) Record the full name of the forest owner.\n(3) Record the number of the citizen identity card or passport of the forest\nowner or of the representative of the family household or residential community.\n(4) Record clearly the address of the forest owner.\n(5) Record the planting zone code, date of grant or number of the certificate of\nsustainable forest management, and the name of the issuing organisation (if any).\nII. CONTENTS OF THE PLAN\n(6) Record information on the main legislative documents and related legal documents.\n(7) Record the subject of harvesting as provided in clause 2 or clause 7 of Article 6 of this\nCircular: for harvesting of planted forests, record the planted species and the year of planting.\n(8) Record the following information: (i) Place of the harvesting area (lot, compartment, sub-zone, commune);\n(ii) Coordinate information (longitude, latitude) at the mid-point of the harvesting lot for forest lots of less\nthan 04 ha, or coordinate information at a minimum of\n04 vertices of the polygon (longitude and latitude) for\nharvesting lots of 04 ha or more, on the VN 2000 coordinate\nsystem or the WGS84 coordinate system in *.GeoJSON format.\nStatistics of the harvesting area by each harvesting lot, compartment, sub-zone and commune.\n(9) Record the harvesting method: selective harvesting, complete clear cutting, strip clear cutting, patch clear cutting.\n(10) Estimated harvesting output:\n- For final harvesting of timber, compile statistics on the number of logs and\nsections harvested and measure and estimate the estimated harvesting volume (m3);\nfor harvesting of non-timber forest plants, compile statistics recording the\nharvesting volume (tonnes, kg) or the number of trees for bamboo and reed species.\n- For principal harvesting and salvage harvesting of timber, the estimated\nharvesting output shall be determined through direct measurement of the harvested\ntrees or through the establishment of typical sample plots, or depending on\nthe actual local conditions, in order to estimate the harvested timber output.\nThe unit of measurement of harvesting output is: kg, m3, ster or number of specimens.\n(11) Solutions for forest restoration after harvesting: state clearly the implementation solutions such as: forest sanitation and reforestation.\nForm No. 09: Request for approval of the plan for harvesting timber and non-timber forest plants of\nordinary species/ordinary forest animals from the wild/collection of specimens of ordinary species.\nAGENCY (1) ....\n-------\nSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF VIETNAM\nIndependence - Freedom - Happiness\n---------------\nNo.: ..../.... ......, day ...... month ..... year ......\nREQUEST FOR APPROVAL OF THE PLAN (*)\n(2) ..................................\nTo(3): .............................................................."
